# A small test level for the Box3D physics example.
#
# A subdivided 12x12 floor, a ramp rising to 3 units, and three low
# walls. The floor is subdivided so that it HAS interior edges -- a
# body sliding across it must not catch on the seams, which is what
# the mesh baker's shared-edge classification exists to prevent.
#
# Winding matters: a Box3D mesh triangle is one-sided, so a surface
# wound the wrong way is one a body falls through rather than one
# that is merely invisible. Surfaces face up, walls face inward.
#
# 1 unit is about 1 metre.

